        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): abort reaps autonomous executor process trees",
        "body": "Closes #104847\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where aborting a CLI-backed agent turn on a service-managed Gateway could stop the visible turn while leaving child processes spawned by the autonomous executor alive. Those survivors could continue acting with the executor's credentials after the operator believed the run had stopped.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe process supervisor now requires callers to declare a typed process role:\n\n- `executor` runs own an independently cancellable process group on POSIX, including service-managed Gateways. If an isolated group cannot be created, startup fails closed instead of falling back to the Gateway's process group.\n- `background` runs preserve the existing daemon/service ownership used by `exec`/`process` sessions and cron exit watchers that may intentionally outlive the initiating turn.\n\nBoth one-shot CLI backend runs and Claude stdio live sessions are marked as executors. The existing chat-abort path already cancels their managed run; this change makes that cancellation reach the executor's child process hierarchy without signaling the Gateway or changing persistent background-session behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can rely on abort to terminate the active CLI executor and its child process hierarchy. Persistent `exec`/`process` background sessions keep their current lifecycle and continue until they exit or are explicitly stopped.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFresh full CI on the current head (`0119396a1e`): https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/29178217948\n\nFocused coverage added:\n\n- `src/process/supervisor/turn-lifecycle.test.ts` starts a real parent/child process hierarchy under the service-managed marker, cancels the executor run, and verifies both PIDs are gone.\n- `src/process/supervisor/adapters/child.test.ts` verifies executors still receive an isolated group in service mode and cannot use the unsafe no-detach fallback.\n- `src/process/supervisor/supervisor.test.ts` verifies the role is retained in run records and forwarded to the child adapter.\n- `src/agents/cli-runner.spawn.test.ts` verifies both one-shot and Claude live CLI paths declare the executor role.\n\nThe preceding full run passed production types, test types, lint, core tests, CLI runner/tool shards, and agent runner shards. Its two unrelated failures were current-main documentation-map and UI i18n baseline drift; this branch was then rebased onto the upstream fixes and regenerated `docs/docs_map.md` from the same ClawHub source used by CI before the fresh run above.\n\nLocal lightweight preflight: targeted `oxfmt`, targeted `oxlint`, and `git diff --check` all passed. Builds and full tests were intentionally run in GitHub Actions.\n\n## Risk And Rollback\n\nThe behavior change is limited to process-supervisor ownership for CLI executors. Windows keeps its existing tree-termination path. POSIX background work retains the existing service-managed behavior. Reverting this commit restores the previous spawn policy and removes the role contract.",
